   "reason": "Quote omitted the operative lead-in 'Specific aspects for vaccines should be addressed in the PSUR'; statement said 'proposed' instead of 'should be addressed'.",
   "row": {
    "statement": "The MAH should address the following vaccine-specific aspects in the PSUR: impact of manufacturing process changes on safety; batch relatedness of adverse reactions and other (quality) problems; vaccine failures/lack of effect; relevant literature on stabilisers, preservatives, adjuvants and products with comparable antigens; concomitant administration with another vaccine where mentioned in the SPC; and safety aspects of different vaccination schedules and dosages (adults, children).",
    "quote": "Specific aspects for vaccines should be addressed in the PSUR:\n\n\n\n1\n See http://www.brightoncollaboration.org/internet/en/index.html.\n\nEMEA/CHMP/PhVWP/372004/2005 Page 4/7\n ©EMEA 2005\n\f o Impact of changes of the manufacturing process on safety;\n o Batch relatedness of adverse reactions and other (quality) problems;\n o Vaccines failures/lack of effect. Reports on vaccine failure/ lack of efficacy should be\n summarised and assessed in a separate chapter;\n o Relevant literature information concerning stabilisers, preservatives and adjuvants and\n products with comparable antigens;\n o Concomitant administration: If concomitant vaccination (either simultaneous or mixed\n administration) with another vaccine is specifically mentioned in the SPC, safety aspects of\n the concomitant administration should be analysed; and\n o Safety aspects of different vaccination schedules and different dosages (adults, children).",
